From 9257e46ea3fd8da4766cfd0dba4b15af56cf0d6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Project <noreply@invalid>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 08:21:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: split late-CPU evidence from commit receipt

Replace the mixed late-CPU attestation with an ABI 3 boundary that
separates fallible per-target evidence, a state-free immutable plan, an
architecture-owned receipt, and a copied READY token.

Describe full target register images and typed CTR, Spectre-v2,
Spectre-v4, BHB, compat-AES, and speculative-AT decisions. Keep the
MT6797 classifier and validator deliberately unresolved, leave the
architecture commit unavailable, and retain both CPU boot and disable
vetoes.

This experiment-only change has no certifying sign-off and is not
submission-ready.
